            <ArticleTitle>[Clinico-instrumental parallels in ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Correlations between coronary angiographic findings and the results of some noninvasive functional tests (electro- and echocardiography, bicycle ergometry, etc.) were examined in 50 patients. A relationship was established between the quantity of essentially (over 50% of the lumen) stenosed major coronary arteries and stress tolerance or the double product.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
